    "buggy_baseline_is_parent": true,
    "single_parent_matches_baseline": true,
    "commit_message": "Recognize CJK full stops in the non-linguistic sentence fallback\n\nOn platforms without NaturalLanguage, BeginDocumentationCommentWithOneLineSummary\napproximated sentences by splitting on ASCII periods only, so a summary ending in\nan ideographic full stop was reported as unterminated. The linguistic path on\nDarwin already treats these characters as sentence terminators, so the two\nimplementations disagreed on the same source.\n\nThe fallback now scans for any full stop, including U+3002, U+FF0E, and U+FF61,\nand ends a sentence at each one. An ASCII period still needs a following space or\nthe end of the text so that decimal points and abbreviations are unaffected.\n\nFixes #1237",
    "boundary_evidence": "repair/boundary-verification.json",
    "boundary_evidence_sha256": "490c51113faece051abeb9083b6f35a48a379b24d0db8592ad205b4d78177aa8"
